# Shader bank (12 October 2026)

Procedural building blocks for every look of a reproduction, the image counterpart of the zenray-height block dataset. A reproduction is never textured with the reference image or with a colour grid sampled from it: every look is a composition of these blocks with measured parameters, fitted on the numpy twins and rendered by the GLSL, sharp 1:1 at any resolution. (12 October 2026)

## One folder per block (12 October 2026)

| File | Content |
|---|---|
| `<id>/block.glsl` | a pure GLSL ES 3.0 function `vec4 <id>(vec2 uv, <params in block.json order>)`; `uv` is the pixel centre in [0,1]^2 with v pointing down; returns straight RGBA in 0..1. Mask blocks return `(1, 1, 1, m)`, colour blocks alpha 1. Helper functions are prefixed `<id>_`. No uniforms inside: every parameter is an argument, so one block can serve several layers. |
| `<id>/twin.py` | `render(params, u, v)`, the same formula vectorised in numpy: HxWx3 float 0..255 (colour block) or HxW float 0..1 (mask block). `u, v` are the pixel-centre grids of `zrmd.shaders.bank.uv_grid`. |
| `<id>/block.json` | `{id, family, description, params:[{name, type, default, min, max, unit}], source_url, licence, attribution, tags, looks}`. Types: `float`, `vec2`, `vec3`, `color` (vec3, sRGB 0..1). `looks` lists the look ids the block can serve. |
| `<id>/thumb.png` | the GLSL render at the default parameters (written by the verifier with `--write-thumbs`). |
| `index.json` | summary of every folder, rebuilt by `zrmd.shaders.bank.rebuild_index()` (the verifier calls it). |

## Licences (12 October 2026)

Code is copied only from MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0, CC0 or public-domain sources, with the exact URL in `source_url` and the licence in `licence`; otherwise the function is written from the mathematics and `licence` starts with `original`. Never Shadertoy code under its default CC BY-NC-SA, never LYGIA (Prosperity licence), never a pixel, logo or text of a reference video. (12 October 2026)

## Commands (12 October 2026)

```bash
cd /Users/zenray/Create/Build/Productions/GithubProductions/ZenRayMotionDesign
~/.venvs/zenray-motion/bin/python -I Scripts/VerifyShaderBank.py --write-thumbs   # GLSL against twin, exit 0 = green
~/.venvs/zenray-motion/bin/python -I Scripts/VerifyShaderBank.py --json           # machine-readable report
~/.venvs/zenray-motion/bin/python -I tests/test_shader_compose.py                  # composition, both ways
```

Python API: `bank.load(id)`, `bank.list_blocks()`, `bank.render_twin(id, params, w, h)`, `bank.render_glsl(ids_and_params, w, h, out_png)`, `bank.render_glsl_batch(compositions, w, h)` (many frames, one browser run), `compose.evaluate(layers, w, h)` and `compose.emit_glsl(layers)`. A layer is `{"block", "params", "blend": normal|add|multiply|screen, "mask": {"block", "params"}}`. Settings (paths, verification size, mean threshold of 2 levels, still fps, browser GPU mode) live in `settings.json`, section `shaders`. (12 October 2026)

## Verification criteria (12 October 2026, S4)

A block is green when, for every case (defaults plus N random in-bounds sets), the mean absolute error between the GLSL render and the numpy twin is at most `shaders.verify_mean_max` (2 levels) AND at most `shaders.verify_outlier_share_max` (0.1 %) of the pixels differ by more than `shaders.verify_outlier_levels` (8 levels) in their worst channel, and its metadata keeps the contract (fields, allowed licence, signature, no em or en dash). The outlier criterion closes the S2 finding: a geometric error confined to a small area (an arc 30 degrees too long) kept a mean of 1.76 levels and passed before. Twins of step functions (dither, grain cells) emulate the GPU's float32 where a floor decides a pixel. (12 October 2026)

## Using the bank in a reproduction (12 October 2026, S4)

1. **Name the look.** Find it in `looks-onekey.json` (measured description, crops, times) and read its line in `looks-onekey-coverage.json`, which lists the blocks that compose it and the structural gaps no block can fill yet. For a new reference, measure its looks the same way first (`Scripts/MeasureLooksOnekey.py` is the pattern). (12 October 2026)
2. **Write the composition as a layer list**, bottom first, in a small script or the version's params: `[{"block": "arch_glow_field", "params": {...}}, {"block": "solid_color", "params": {...}, "mask": {"block": "sdf_circle", "params": {...}}}, {"block": "glow_ring", "blend": "add", "params": {...}}]`. Colour blocks fill, mask blocks cut (`mask`), glows go in `add` or `screen`, vignettes in `multiply`. Seed the parameters with the measured values of the look (colours from the S1 hex medians, sizes in canvas heights). (12 October 2026)
3. **Fit on the twins, never on the GPU.** Build a residual `compose.evaluate(layers(x), w, h) - target` on a crop of the reference (the crop is analysis data, it never becomes a texture) and run `scipy.optimize.least_squares` with multi-start on the shape parameters. Reference implementation: `Scripts/FitArchGlowBank.py` (screen crops from a device3d version, 18 starts on 16 processes, refine, report RMS per frame). (12 October 2026)
4. **Render the same description as GLSL.** `compose.emit_glsl(layers)` gives one fragment shader and its uniforms; `bank.render_glsl_batch([layers], W, H)` renders it at any size through HyperFrames. Check GLSL against `compose.evaluate` (mean under 1 level), then render the final size: the result is code, sharp 1:1 at any resolution. (12 October 2026)
5. **Animate by parameters.** A look that moves over time is a track of parameter values per frame (fitted frame by frame with a warm start, or driven by an ease block), never a sequence of images. (12 October 2026)
6. **A missing block is written, not faked.** Add it to a generator (`Scripts/HarvestShapesLight.py`, `Scripts/HarvestNoisePost.py`, `Scripts/HarvestCriticGaps.py`, each owns its folders through a marker), run `Scripts/VerifyShaderBank.py --blocks <id> --sets 6 --write-thumbs`, prove it red once on a scratch copy (`ZRMD_SHADER_BANK=<copy>`), and add its id to the look in `looks-onekey-coverage.json`. A block that fails and cannot be fixed moves to `_quarantine/<id>/` with a `QUARANTINE.md` note; nothing is deleted. (12 October 2026)

Current limits, all listed per look in `looks-onekey-coverage.json`: `compose` has no filter layer (grade, blur or mirror of an arbitrary composite needs render to texture), glyph and logo masks come from the typography layer, and mesh lighting stays in `templates/device3d`. (12 October 2026)
